        "question": {
            "id": 25,
            "category": "debugging",
            "intent": "parallel_tool_interrupt_collection_and_resume",
            "difficulty": "very_hard",
            "question": "A ToolNode executes multiple tool calls in parallel, and each tool reaches interrupt(). Explain the complete lifecycle of those interrupts from the point where interrupt() raises inside each tool through their representation in Pregel task state and the checkpoint, including how each pending interrupt is associated with the task that raised it. Then explain how Command(resume={interrupt_id: value}) is matched against those pending interrupts, and distinguish the task identity used by the runtime from the namespace-derived Interrupt.id. Finally, explain under what conditions two parallel tasks could expose the same interrupt ID and why that would make the resume map ambiguous.",
            "expected_files": [
                "interrupts.mdx",
                "langgraph/langgraph/types.py",
                "prebuilt/langgraph/prebuilt/tool_node.py",
                "prebuilt/langgraph/prebuilt/interrupt.py",
                "langgraph/langgraph/pregel/_loop.py",
                "langgraph/langgraph/pregel/_algo.py",
                "langgraph/langgraph/pregel/_runner.py"
            ],
            "concepts": [
                "ToolNode",
                "parallel execution",
                "interrupt exceptions",
                "Pregel tasks",
                "pending interrupts",
                "checkpoint state",
                "task identity",
                "interrupt namespace",
                "Interrupt.id",
                "resume mapping"
            ],
            "tags": [
                "ToolNode",
                "parallel_interrupts",
                "pending_interrupts",
                "resume",
                "task_mapping",
                "interrupt_namespace",
                "interrupt_id"
            ],
            "code_snippet": "from langgraph.prebuilt import ToolNode\nfrom langgraph.types import interrupt, Command\nfrom langgraph.checkpoint.memory import InMemorySaver\n\n\ndef create_circle():\n    return interrupt({\"tool\": \"circle\", \"question\": \"approve circle?\"})\n\ndef create_square():\n    return interrupt({\"tool\": \"square\", \"question\": \"approve square?\"})\n\ndef create_triangle():\n    return interrupt({\"tool\": \"triangle\", \"question\": \"approve triangle?\"})\n\n# A ToolNode receives three tool calls in the same graph step.\n# All three tools reach interrupt().\n# The application reads graph.get_state(config).tasks and constructs:\n# Command(resume={interrupt_id: response})",
            "observed_behavior": "Three parallel tool executions reach interrupt(), and the application must preserve the association between each pending interrupt, its originating task, and the resume value used to continue it.",
            "expected_behavior": "The answer should trace how interrupts raised by parallel ToolNode tasks are propagated and collected, how pending interrupts are represented in task/checkpoint state, how the originating task and interrupt namespace contribute to interrupt identity, and how Command(resume={interrupt_id: value}) uses that identity to associate a resume value with the correct pending interrupt. It should also explain why duplicate interrupt IDs can make the resume map ambiguous even when the underlying tasks are distinct.",
            "error": null,
            "logs": null,
            "evidence": null,
            "queries": [
                "How does ToolNode execute multiple tool calls concurrently and create separate execution tasks?",
                "How are interrupt exceptions raised inside parallel tool executions collected by the Pregel runner?",
                "How are pending interrupts stored in Pregel task state and checkpoint state?",
                "How is a pending interrupt associated with the task that originally raised it?",
                "How does Command(resume={interrupt_id: value}) map a resume value to a pending interrupt and its originating task?",
                "How is Interrupt.id derived from the execution namespace, and how is that different from the runtime task identity?",
                "Under what conditions can parallel tasks have the same interrupt namespace or Interrupt.id?",
                "Why do duplicate interrupt IDs make a resume map ambiguous even when the underlying tasks are distinct?"
            ]
        },
